# Update References when adding content

When adding or changing **public research claims** under `site/` (or promoting a draft into `site/`):

1. Add every **new material primary or secondary URL** used on-page to [`site/references.html`](site/references.html) in the right subsection (`#wb-ida`, `#mega-projects`, `#secondary-us`, GoC list, etc.), or create a subsection if needed.
2. Same PR / same commit set as the content change — do **not** defer References to a follow-up.
3. Prefer GoC / institutional primaries for legal KPIs; label secondary clearly; never host Investor Guide or other third-party PDFs under `site/` / `public/`.
4. Mirror the change in [`docs/CONTENT_CHANGELOG.md`](docs/CONTENT_CHANGELOG.md) **Sources** line and [`site/changelog.html`](site/changelog.html) when the public page set changes.
5. Exceptions: pure typography / CSS / nav chrome with **no new citations**; updating display text only for an already-listed URL.

Cross-check: [`docs/PRE_PUSH_GATE.md`](docs/PRE_PUSH_GATE.md) researcher checklist remains authoritative for humans.
